[
    {
        "content": "<p>Hello, I am quite new to Lean, and as a fun project I decided to try to formalise propositional formulas from the ground. I am trying to define them in terms of atomic propositions and the logical connectives, but I am running into an issue. My approach so far is the following: </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"c\">/-</span><span class=\"cm\"> P is the type of propositional atoms -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Form</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">atom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">not</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Form</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">and</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ψ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Form</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">or</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ψ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Form</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">imp</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ψ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Form</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I would like to view each (p : P) as an element of Form P, so I define a coercion: </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Coe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Form</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">coe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Form</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">atom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>In the following example, this works well:<br>\n<code>example (φ : Form P) (p : P) := φ.and p</code><br>\nHowever, the next example does not work<br>\n<code>example (p q : P) := Form.and p q</code>.<br>\nWhy are p and q not coerced to Form P in the second example?</p>",
        "id": 586347370,
        "sender_full_name": "RobQnadqs",
        "timestamp": 1776587818
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>As a followup question: I would actually like to implement the atomic propositions not as a variable type as input to the Form type, but as a fixed type, because this current definition allows for the type Form Nat, for example, which feels strange. But I dont know how I would define this, because there is no concrete definition. In a sense, I want to create a sort of \"free type\", which is fixed but arbitrary; A type that I declare to exists without saying anything more about it. Is something like this possible in Lean?</p>",
        "id": 586347780,
        "sender_full_name": "RobQnadqs",
        "timestamp": 1776588258
    },
    {
        "content": "<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">AtomType</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">AtomType</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">AtomType</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Form</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">atom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">not</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Form</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">and</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ψ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Form</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">or</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ψ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Form</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">imp</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ψ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Form</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Coe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Form</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">coe</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">atom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Form</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">and</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">P</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Form</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">and</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">q</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 586355602,
